00:05:34.440 --> 00:05:40.620
I never actually single-handedly saved a girl from drowning by abseiling bare-chested into the river. That-

00:05:40.660 --> 00:05:42.620
That was Rob's version of the story.

00:05:42.620 --> 00:05:48.420
Secondly, previous predictions of sea level rise actually match up fairly well with what we've observed

00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:51.100
The very first IPCC report in 1990

00:05:51.140 --> 00:05:54.960
made a series of predictions of sea-level rise by the present day

00:05:54.960 --> 00:05:59.800
and satellite observations are right in the middle of their predictions for the first 26 years,

00:05:59.800 --> 00:06:03.820
showing slightly less sea level rise than their best guess at the time

00:06:03.820 --> 00:06:07.880
Current estimates still have uncertainties attached but much smaller ones as we

00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:13.340
understand the systems much better and as our models for predicting sea level rise add new complexity

00:06:13.340 --> 00:06:18.720
and more physical systems, our estimates as well as getting more accurate get higher and higher

00:06:18.720 --> 00:06:24.260
It's considered very likely that sea levels in the year 2100 will be between 30 and

00:06:24.260 --> 00:06:28.200
130 centimeters higher than in the year 2000

00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:33.020
And a lot of scientists consider that to be too conservative an estimate. In other words,

00:06:33.020 --> 00:06:40.020
the acceleration of sea level rise that we've observed humans calls to date, is only the thin end of the wedge

00:06:40.060 --> 00:06:45.240
Sea levels are going to rise faster and faster every decade and by the end of the century,

00:06:45.240 --> 00:06:50.260
the impacts are going to be very real. So to answer the question in the video's title

00:06:50.260 --> 00:06:57.800
Sea levels HAVE been rising every decade. And in fact, the sea level has been rising faster every decade

00:06:57.800 --> 00:07:00.700
Scientists understand the physical systems behind this increase in sea level

00:07:00.700 --> 00:07:04.800
and have seen their prediction born out by   observations thus far,

00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:10.540
And the acceleration of sea level rise that we, humans, cause is going to continue for the foreseeable future

00:07:10.700 --> 00:07:16.020
committing us to potentially more than a meter of sea level rise by the end of the century

